FILE = "jensen-huang-reinstated-nvidia-ceo.html"
TITLE = "Jensen Huang is back as Nvidia CEO, 11 days after resigning"
TAG = "The Wrap"
H1 = "Jensen Huang is back as Nvidia CEO, 11 days after resigning"
DEK = "The board that ruled out his return last week has voted unanimously to bring him back, saying it got assurances from the US government that his return poses no national security risk."
META = "The Wrap · Global · 23 Nov 2026 · 3 min read"
LEAD = ("img/wr-jensen-huang.jpg", "Jensen Huang", "NVIDIA")

BODY = [
("p", "Jensen Huang is running Nvidia again. The chipmaker's board said on Monday, 23 November, that it had reinstated him as president, CEO and board member, effective immediately. The vote was unanimous. The news came out shortly before 5pm Kenya time, just 11 days after Huang stepped down from the company he co-founded and had led for 33 years."),
("p", "Huang resigned on 12 November. It followed reports that he had extramarital affairs, one of them with Alice Huang, a businesswoman US officials suspect of having links to Chinese intelligence. She used to be an executive at Megaspeed, a Singapore-based company that US authorities are investigating over the possible diversion of Nvidia chips to China. Megaspeed has denied the allegations. CFO Colette Kress took over as interim CEO."),
("h2", "", "A sharp ", "U-turn"),
("p", "At Nvidia's earnings call last week, the board said it did not intend to bring Huang back, even after he had said publicly that he would return if asked. Over the weekend, the board said it had held a series of discussions and meetings with him. It came away satisfied with his candour and his ability to lead, and it says senior figures in the US government gave it the input that his return poses no national security risk."),
("p", "“The Board believes Jensen is the right person to lead NVIDIA,” said board chair Harvey C. Jones. Huang says he is taking the job back “with the greatest humility and renewed commitment.”"),
("h2", "", "Not over ", "yet"),
("p", "The scandal hasn't gone away, though. An independent board committee is still investigating, with outside lawyers, and Huang has committed to cooperating with it. Last week Nvidia also set up a National Security and Export Control Oversight Committee, which will oversee how the company handles trade compliance and national security risks, and it is now looking for a new Chief Compliance Officer. In Washington, three House committees have called Huang in for a closed-door interview about the affair."),
("p", "For now, the market is happy: Nvidia shares jumped more than 25% before trading opened on Monday. Colette Kress goes back to focusing on her job as CFO."),
]

